WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.653
In this lesson, you will learn to resize
two windows that sit side by side,

00:00:06.653 --> 00:00:07.584
in one gesture.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:10.230
A Layout is a starting point, not a cage.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.751
When your code needs more width for a
moment,

00:00:12.751 --> 00:00:14.991
you should not have to rebuild anything.

00:00:16.355 --> 00:00:19.951
These two windows are Snapped side by
side, each in its own Zone.

00:00:20.422 --> 00:00:23.209
The line where they meet is called a
Shared edge.

00:00:23.209 --> 00:00:25.769
Point at it, exactly where the windows
touch.

00:00:26.408 --> 00:00:31.373
Now drag it to the right. Watch the window
on the right: it follows as you drag.

00:00:31.373 --> 00:00:33.296
There is no gap and no overlap.

00:00:33.652 --> 00:00:37.852
It works in both directions. Drag back,
and the other window grows again.

00:00:38.315 --> 00:00:41.468
Only the windows change. The Layout stays
as it is.

00:00:41.987 --> 00:00:44.584
So your next Snap uses the original Zones.

00:00:44.584 --> 00:00:47.861
To go back to the plan, simply Snap the
window again.

00:00:49.335 --> 00:00:50.731
This is on by default.

00:00:50.731 --> 00:00:53.204
To turn it off, open Settings, General,

00:00:53.204 --> 00:00:56.185
and clear Resize neighbouring windows
together.

00:00:57.833 --> 00:00:59.776
Some examples of a quick rebalance.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:04.359
You are reading a long function: give the
editor more width for a moment,

00:01:04.359 --> 00:01:06.679
and the documentation beside it shrinks.

00:01:07.029 --> 00:01:12.126
A web page that needs more room: widen the
browser, read, and drag the edge back.

00:01:12.476 --> 00:01:16.863
It works with more than two windows: two
stacked windows both follow the edge of

00:01:16.863 --> 00:01:18.399
the tall window beside them.

00:01:19.949 --> 00:01:24.944
To recap. Drag the edge where two Snapped
windows meet, and both resize together.

00:01:24.944 --> 00:01:29.817
Your Layout does not change, and Snapping
again brings back the original Zones.

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:34.271
In the next lesson, you will learn to make
your own Layouts.
